From 5b1fcd3d81cdef51d26cf5e5069fe07a3367397e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:23:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 53/57] hw/misc: EMC2301 fan controller with a fan, the Fan
 Click

emc2301 at I2C 0x2F drives a modelled four-wire fan: Direct Setting and
the RPM-based algorithm (update period, gain, Max Step, Minimum Drive,
error window), spin-up, stall, spin and drive-fail status cleared on
read once their cause is gone, the four-second power-up watchdog, the
software lock, and ALERT#. The fan's speed follows its duty with a lag;
TACH Reading comes from it by the data sheet's equation 4-2. qtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
