+  ALERT# on INT (R3 10k pull-up), and a four-wire fan on its terminals.
+  Direct Setting and the RPM-based algorithm (update period, gain, Max
+  Step, Minimum Drive, error window), spin-up, stall, spin and drive-fail
+  status, the four-second power-up watchdog, the software lock, and TACH
+  Reading from the fan's speed by the data sheet's equation 4-2. The fan
+  follows ``max-rpm`` (4000) times its duty with a ``tau-ms`` (700) lag,
+  stops below ``min-duty`` (200 per mille) or while ``blocked``; ``rpm``
+  and ``duty`` read what it does.
